WEBVTT

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.200
You always forget to buy something.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.070
Then you tell me "Hey Kazuma, can you go and buy something for me?"

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.250
Kazuma...

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.180
Kazuma!

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:37.380
What am I saying?

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:39.310
So embarrassing!

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.820
I want him to call me Yui, too.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:47.070
Aoi Yui, age 12.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:51.740
I admire those who can call their boyfriend by his first name.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.490
Ready, action!

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.540
Those dreamy eyes and full lips...

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:48.950
...are mine alone, Hanabi...

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:52.060
Cut!

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:55.170
Be more like a wild beast!

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:58.500
Hey boys, stop!

00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.730
Eikou!

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:02.450
Time to run away! Run, run!

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:10.620
Jeez! The boys only know how to mess around!

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:15.970
This is delicious!

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:18.350
Does anyone want more juice?

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:19.440
Here!

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.350
Me too!

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:23.450
Hey, listen!

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:27.620
I have someone I like!

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:33.190
I thought we were just friends,

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:35.380
but when he called me by my first name...

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:37.670
My heart skipped a beat!

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:40.440
Eh? He suddenly called you by your first name?

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:45.340
Takao never called me Hanabi yet.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:46.600
Really?

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:51.390
Even though you've been on dates and gave each other birthday presents?

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:52.200
Yeah!

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.860
We've been calling each other Takao and Ayase.

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:58.140
Hiyama hasn't called me by my first name either.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:00.800
I call him by his last name, too.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.900
Really?

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:06.620
I thought you all were only doing that in public.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:12.840
Couples have their own special ways of calling each other.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:15.250
Really?

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:20.200
My sister always calls her new boyfriends by their first names.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:22.250
It deepens their relationship, she says.

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:23.620
First name...

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:26.060
Kazuma...

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:30.820
Kazuma.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:36.330
But names aren't anything special.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:39.860
It's the fact that you're calling each other by your first names.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:41.150
Yes, yes!

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:45.770
I feel so blessed when we call each other by our first names.

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:49.490
How nice.

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:55.930
I wonder if Takao will be happy if I call him by his first name.

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:00.220
Yuuto.

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:03.800
I love you, Hanabi.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:06.940
How nice!

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:11.860
Miss Marin, I want Takao to call me by my first name, too!

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:18.360
Oh my. Why don't you ask him in a cute voice, "Call me Hanabi!"

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:21.610
I want him to call me naturally.

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:25.110
"Call me Hanabi." "Okay." I don't want it to be like that.

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:26.700
I understand completely!

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:28.690
Yeah, yeah!

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:32.810
I want to call Hiyama by his first name, too.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:34.540
I want him to call me by my first name, too.

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:36.760
Just try, Yui.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:39.580
You like him, right?

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:43.140
Yes, but it's embarrassing.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:45.940
A girl in love needs to make her move!

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:47.820
How about me?

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:50.170
You're right.

00:05:50.170 --> 00:05:53.220
Why don't you casually bring it up?

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:58.400
Call yourself by your first name accidentally and see what happens.

00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:02.680
Takao is pretty sensitive about things like that, so I'm sure he'll notice.

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:04.950
I got it! I'll try it out!

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:08.230
I'll try calling him by his first name, too.

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:10.380
Yui! Hanabi!

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:12.600
Go for it, you two!

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.360
Okay!

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:19.760
U-Um...

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:23.910
Would you l-like to go home together today?

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:28.980
K-K-Kazu-

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:32.810
I just can't say it!

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:50.730
Why don't you casually bring it up?

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:55.910
Takao, what book are you reading?

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:59.100
I... Hanabi is curious!

00:06:59.100 --> 00:06:59.830
Hmm?

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:03.840
Hanabi would like to read it, too!

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:05.320
Hanabi...

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:08.710
Would you like to read it after I'm finished?

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:15.230
Miss Marin!

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:18.280
What's wrong, my lost kitten?

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:22.040
I kept calling myself by my first name today!

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:24.890
H-Hanabi!

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:28.140
Hanabi!

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:31.140
H-Hanabi...

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.400
But he ignored them all!

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:37.410
Hanabi, I failed today, too.

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:38.750
Yui!

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:40.150
Hanabi!

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:42.420
Then how about this!

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:45.700
Yuuto! What great weather we have today!

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:49.760
Takao will notice that you're calling him by his first name!

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:51.720
You're right, Hanabi.

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:53.400
That's great!

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:56.620
Timing's important here.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:08:00.030
Just tell him something he likes.

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:02.130
That way your chances of success goes up!

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:04.740
I heard all about it, Hiyama!

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:08.350
You got a cell phone, right?

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:09.940
That has nothing to do with you.

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:13.390
My parents are on a trip so they're letting me use theirs.

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:16.160
I don't care if you only have it for a little bit! Please give me your email!

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:17.420
Me too!

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:20.080
Hiyama has a cell phone?

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:23.580
You should ask him for his email, too!

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:27.160
You can easily email him using his first name.

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:29.070
Emailing Hiyama?

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:31.560
I've never thought about it before.

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:35.480
Sounds nice.

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:42.120
I don't have a cell phone, but I can email you using the computer in my house!

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:44.470
I don't have a computer, but I can keep your email around.

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:46.850
Hiyama, your email...

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:48.980
Hiyama, tell me already!

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:50.660
Um, Hiyama...

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:52.560
Tell me your email!

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:55.000
Hurry up!

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:58.130
Shut up! I won't give it to anyone!

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:09.750
So he won't give it to me?

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:12.130
That's possible with Hiyama.

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:16.050
Hey, here you go.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:26.270
An email address?

00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:29.130
It's my mom's, so it's only temporary.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:31.540
I thought you weren't giving it to anyone.

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:34.450
You're an exception.

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:46.260
Aoi Yui, age 12.

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:50.550
My boyfriend made an exception for me!

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:12.020
My first email, I'm a bit nervous. Aoi.

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:15.100
My heart is beating so fast!

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:24.180
It sent!

00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:39.040
He replied!

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:52.900
Good morning!

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:57.240
You read so many books already!

00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:58.500
Wow!

00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:02.260
Oh! Now's a great chance to call him by his first name!

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:06.740
Ayase?

00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:10.570
You're amazing...

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:14.880
Y-Yuuto...

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:26.950
Thank you, Ayase.

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:36.950
Seems like Takao is denser than usual.

00:11:36.950 --> 00:11:40.170
Well then, time for our trump card! Operation Kenta!

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:42.940
Kenta? Who's that?

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:49.160
Hey, Takao, my friend Kenta is amazing!

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:50.220
Kenta?

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:52.630
He'll become jealous!

00:11:52.630 --> 00:11:55.010
W-Who is he, Hanabi?

00:11:55.010 --> 00:11:57.920
He doesn't want to lose so he calls you directly by your first name!

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:03.410
What a plan, but I've never called any of the other boys by their first names.

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:06.600
Just make up some guy.

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:08.530
My sister does that a lot.

00:12:08.530 --> 00:12:11.330
Thanks, but I'm fine.

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:15.480
I don't want to lie to Takao, so Kenta...

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:16.040
Kenta?

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:19.790
Takao! When did you start listening?

00:12:19.790 --> 00:12:21.130
Just now.

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:24.600
It's rare for you to call a guy by his first name.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:26.260
No, uh...

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:27.940
Isn't this a great chance?

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:30.060
You get along well with others.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:32.440
Here it is! The jealousy!

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:36.030
H...

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:42.800
Hurry on back to class since lunch break is ending soon.

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:43.640
Ayase...

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:48.040
Ayase...

00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:53.000
Let's have a duel.

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:58.180
We'll see who can read more books and write more book comments.

00:12:58.180 --> 00:13:01.120
The one who loses has to listen to the winner.

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:02.260
How about it?

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:08.340
Sure, I accept.

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:13.300
I'll just force him to call me by my first name then!

00:13:28.360 --> 00:13:32.780
Any developments, you two lovebirds?

00:13:32.780 --> 00:13:35.110
We've been emailing each other.

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:37.320
How about you, Hanabi?

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:41.320
I guess nothing's happened.

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:45.080
It's fine, it's fine. A focused girl is cute, too.

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:46.950
Let me see your love emails!

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:49.670
Is that okay?

00:13:49.670 --> 00:13:52.470
Share with me some of your happiness.

00:13:54.510 --> 00:13:56.020
Did you make your schedule yet?

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:56.860
Yeah!

00:13:56.860 --> 00:13:59.270
P.E. tomorrow is basketball.

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:00.560
Got it.

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:02.550
Don't forget to do your homework.

00:14:02.550 --> 00:14:03.580
Got it!

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:08.460
Are you his mom!?

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:11.900
Isn't this lovely?

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:14.670
Lovely? How!?

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:18.310
Well, I used heart smileys.

00:14:18.310 --> 00:14:24.610
My sister said that you can talk about things in emails that you can't talk about directly.

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:28.170
Do you have anything you want to say to Hiyama?

00:14:30.210 --> 00:14:31.500
I do!

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:51.040
It's embarrassing... But I want to tell him!

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:54.600
I love you, Kazuma!

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:20.840
Not him.

00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:28.680
Oh, jeez!

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:37.690
Why isn't he replying?

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:46.990
I wonder if he's mad since I called him by his first name randomly.

00:15:46.990 --> 00:15:49.090
I don't think that's it.

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:51.050
Miss Marin!

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:54.460
What's up so early in the morning, my lost sheep?

00:15:54.460 --> 00:15:55.700
Actually...

00:15:55.700 --> 00:15:57.990
I'll go on ahead.

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:06.110
Hiyama, my email yesterday...

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:10.450
My cell phone? My parents came back yesterday, so I gave it back.

00:16:10.450 --> 00:16:12.440
So you didn't check your email?

00:16:12.440 --> 00:16:15.020
Email? Did you send something yesterday?

00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:17.540
You should at least tell me when you're giving it back!

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:19.580
You lack any tact, Hiyama!

00:16:23.860 --> 00:16:27.620
Are you an idiot? You're getting so mad over an email.

00:16:28.060 --> 00:16:31.340
You're an idiot! I hate you!

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:41.280
Takao! Today's the end of our duel, right?

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:42.620
You're right.

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:46.740
I worked hard! You'll call me by my first name!

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:48.590
One, two.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:51.470
I lost!

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:55.310
But you were close.

00:16:55.310 --> 00:16:57.970
I tried too hard, too.

00:16:57.970 --> 00:17:01.660
You read a lot of books, Ayase.

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:05.860
You could have read lighter books since we were competing in number.

00:17:06.730 --> 00:17:10.480
Oh yeah! I screwed up!

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:13.370
You never thought about that, right?

00:17:13.370 --> 00:17:17.040
The loser has to listen to the winner, right?

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:18.910
Y-Yes.

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:21.380
Tell me why you wanted this duel.

00:17:21.380 --> 00:17:23.310
I'll make your wish come true.

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:26.920
Eh?

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:32.160
Another quote so early in the morning!

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:34.060
"I'll make your wish come true."

00:17:35.850 --> 00:17:39.630
Then can you walk home with me today?

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:44.280
Eh? You worked so hard for just that?

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:45.850
That's not all!

00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:48.340
I'm really happy if we can walk home together!

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:52.460
I can't say it. I lost anyway.

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:59.260
But one day when I become more mature, I'll make sure he calls me Hanabi.

00:18:00.210 --> 00:18:01.500
Hanabi.

00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:06.090
Takao!

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:09.280
The fireworks (Hanabi) festival is happening again this year.

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:11.720
Fireworks festival?

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:17.940
Oh dear! I thought he was calling me by my first name! I was so happy, too!

00:18:17.940 --> 00:18:21.830
It's really nothing to call her by her first name...

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:25.300
Would you like to go together?

00:18:25.300 --> 00:18:30.820
But her reaction is so cute. Let me just enjoy this for a while longer.

00:18:42.070 --> 00:18:46.640
Hiyama really doesn't understand a girl's heart.

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:49.350
Yui, don't worry about it.

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:50.470
Okay.

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:53.410
I didn't want it to become like this.

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:58.840
I just wanted to tell him what I felt through email.

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:07.660
I don't want this to go on.

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:09.900
I'll go talk to Hiyama.

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:11.720
Do your best, Yui!

00:19:11.720 --> 00:19:13.520
I'm sure it'll go well!

00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:15.310
Thanks, Hanabi.

00:19:15.310 --> 00:19:17.380
You should hurry!

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:22.670
Hiyama gave his cell phone back to his mom, so she may have seen the email!

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:47.000
Hiyama!

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:49.500
Did you see the email?

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:51.010
I just saw it.

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:57.200
This is so embarrassing! I didn't want him to see it now!

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:02.960
But he got it.

00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:06.550
I'm sorry.

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:14.980
That email... Or rather, I thought you were looking down on my feelings.

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:19.040
I said something mean.

00:20:19.370 --> 00:20:25.140
I couldn't answer your feelings.

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:32.450
I'm not used to using email to talk about how I feel, I guess.

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:38.470
I see. It can't be helped.

00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:39.980
That's why!

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:45.720
Just call me! I'll go see you instead of emailing you.

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:49.530
Anytime! Anywhere!

00:20:59.720 --> 00:21:00.730
Okay!

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:07.670
Here's my response.

00:21:11.730 --> 00:21:14.530
I love you too.

00:21:16.720 --> 00:21:17.580
Yui.

00:21:26.150 --> 00:21:29.230
Say it again! Again!

00:21:29.230 --> 00:21:31.840
I don't think I can say it ever again.

00:21:31.840 --> 00:21:33.540
Ever again?

00:21:35.730 --> 00:21:38.300
Aoi Yui, age 12.

00:21:38.860 --> 00:21:42.950
I love my name even more now.

00:23:17.700 --> 00:23:22.970
Yui! How did it feel to be called by your first name?

00:23:23.750 --> 00:23:29.970
I feel like it's like the first time, even though it's my first name.

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:33.920
I love my name even more now.

00:23:33.920 --> 00:23:36.740
How nice, Yui.

00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:43.520
Aoi and Ayase have been acting weird lately.

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:45.820
I don't really understand girls,

00:23:45.820 --> 00:23:48.200
but I can't just leave them alone in pain like this.

00:23:48.200 --> 00:23:50.410
Eh? They fought?

00:23:50.410 --> 00:23:52.650
Next time we'll make everyone's hearts...

00:23:52.650 --> 00:23:54.670
Hey! Now's not the time for that!

00:23:54.670 --> 00:23:56.070
What should we do?
